An investment firm must ensure that trades it undertakes in shares admitted to trading on a regulated market or traded on a trading venue take place on one of the following [MiFIR | Article 23 (Trading obligation for investment firms), p. 34]:

*   A regulated market;
*   A multilateral trading facility (MTF);
*   A systematic internaliser; or
*   A third-country trading venue assessed as equivalent in accordance with Article 25(4)(a) of Directive 2014/65/EU.

These requirements do not apply if the trades are non-systematic, ad-hoc, irregular, and infrequent, or if they are carried out between eligible and/or professional counterparties and do not contribute to the price discovery process [MiFIR | Article 23 (Trading obligation for investment firms), p. 34].
